IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- coa28-sch1c.l4: Schedule 1C (Rules of the Takeover Panel: general principles and other provision), paragraphs 1 to 21,
-- lines 18946-19081 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Section 943 (coa21) makes the Panel's rules give effect to this Schedule. Most
-- paragraphs say what "Rules must ensure": each function here answers what the Act requires the rules to require
-- (or, for Part 1, what the principle says), on facts about the bid; none answers what the Takeover Code itself says,
-- which is outside the sources. Paragraphs that only say what rules "may" provide are rule-making powers: inert.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words (FALSE-kind comments), NOTHING
-- otherwise (NOTHING-kind comments). "must not ... unless" and "must announce only after" are BAR functions: JUST TRUE
-- means the bar holds. A bare "must" that has not been done is answered JUST FALSE by the function that asks whether
-- it has been met (fork F3 in NOTES.md).

-- Who is told on behalf of the employees: the text says "the representatives of their respective employees, or where
-- there are no such representatives, the employees themselves" in paragraphs 11(3), 12(3), 16(b) and 18(2).
DECLARE `sch 1C who is told on behalf of the employees` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C the representatives of the employees`
    `sch 1C the employees themselves`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- PART 1: GENERAL PRINCIPLES (paragraphs 1 to 6)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:19069 | (2) For the purposes of this Schedule, securities are of one class if the rights attached to them are in all respects uniform; and for that purpose the rights attached to securities are not regarded as different from those attached to other securities by reason only that they do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment.
@ref sch 1C para 20(2) Interpretation (src:19069)
GIVEN `the rights attached to the securities are in all respects uniform, disregarding any difference only in the rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(2) the securities are of one class` MEANS
    IF `the rights attached to the securities are in all respects uniform, disregarding any difference only in the rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "securities are of one class if the rights attached to them are in all respects uniform" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:18949 | 1 (1) All holders of the securities of an offeree company of the same class must be afforded equivalent treatment.
@ref sch 1C para 1(1) General principles (src:18949)
GIVEN `the holders hold securities of an offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities are of the same class` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 1(1) the rules must afford the holders equivalent treatment` MEANS
    IF `the holders hold securities of an offeree company` AND `the securities are of the same class` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All holders of the securities of an offeree company of the same class"

-- src:18950 | (2) If a person acquires control of a company, the other holders of securities must be protected.
@ref sch 1C para 1(2) General principles (src:18950)
GIVEN `a person acquires control of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 1(2) the rules must protect the other holders of securities` MEANS
    IF `a person acquires control of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person acquires control of a company, the other holders of securities must be protected" (a failed "if")

-- src:18951 | 2 (1) The holders of the securities of an offeree company must have sufficient time and information to enable them to reach a properly informed decision on the takeover bid.
@ref sch 1C para 2(1) General principles (src:18951)
GIVEN `the holders hold securities of an offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 2(1) the holders must have sufficient time and information to reach a properly informed decision on the takeover bid` MEANS
    IF `the holders hold securities of an offeree company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The holders of the securities of an offeree company"

DECLARE `sch 1C para 2(2) effect` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 2(2)(a) employment`
    `sch 1C para 2(2)(b) conditions of employment`
    `sch 1C para 2(2)(c) the locations of the company's places of business`
    `sch 1C para 2(2) another effect`

-- src:18952 | (2) Where it advises the holders of securities, the board of directors of the offeree company must give its views on the effects of implementation of the takeover bid on—
-- src:18953 | (a) employment,
-- src:18954 | (b) conditions of employment, and
-- src:18955 | (c) the locations of the company’s places of business.
@ref sch 1C para 2(2) General principles (src:18952-18955)
GIVEN `the board advises the holders of securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      effect IS A `sch 1C para 2(2) effect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 2(2) the board of the offeree company must give its views on the effect of implementation of the takeover bid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the board advises the holders of securities`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it advises the holders of securities" (a failed "where")
        IF effect EQUALS `sch 1C para 2(2) another effect`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the effects in (a) to (c) are not closed with "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18956 | 3 The board of directors of an offeree company must act in the interests of the company as a whole and must not deny the holders of securities the opportunity to decide on the merits of the takeover bid.
@ref sch 1C para 3 General principles (src:18956)
GIVEN `the board is the board of directors of an offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board acts in the interests of the company as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board denies the holders of securities the opportunity to decide on the merits of the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 3 the board of the offeree company complies with the principle` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the board is the board of directors of an offeree company`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The board of directors of an offeree company"
        IF `the board acts in the interests of the company as a whole` AND NOT (`the board denies the holders of securities the opportunity to decide on the merits of the takeover bid`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must act in the interests of the company as a whole and must not deny the holders of securities the opportunity to decide on the merits of the takeover bid" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `sch 1C para 4 company concerned` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 4(a) the offeree company`
    `sch 1C para 4(b) the offeror, if the offeror is a company`
    `sch 1C para 4(c) any other company concerned by the takeover bid`
    `sch 1C para 4 another person`

-- src:18957 | 4 False markets must not be created in the securities of—
-- src:18958 | (a) the offeree company,
-- src:18959 | (b) if the offeror is a company, that company, or
-- src:18960 | (c) any other company concerned by the takeover bid,
-- src:18961 | in such a way that the rise or fall of the prices of the securities becomes artificial and the normal functioning of the markets is distorted.
@ref sch 1C para 4 General principles (src:18957-18961)
GIVEN company IS A `sch 1C para 4 company concerned`
      `the offeror is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rise or fall of the prices of the securities becomes artificial and the normal functioning of the markets is distorted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 4 the creation of a false market in the securities of the company is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF company EQUALS `sch 1C para 4 another person`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "False markets must not be created in the securities of— (a) the offeree company, (b) ..., or (c) any other company concerned by the takeover bid"
        IF company EQUALS `sch 1C para 4(b) the offeror, if the offeror is a company` AND NOT (`the offeror is a company`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the offeror is a company, that company" (a failed "if")
        IF `the rise or fall of the prices of the securities becomes artificial and the normal functioning of the markets is distorted`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in such a way that the rise or fall of the prices of the securities becomes artificial and the normal functioning of the markets is distorted"

-- "must announce a takeover bid only after": a bar until (a) and (b) are done.
-- src:18962 | 5 An offeror must announce a takeover bid only after—
-- src:18963 | (a) ensuring that the offeror can fulfil in full any cash consideration, if such is offered, and
-- src:18964 | (b) taking all reasonable measures to secure the implementation of any other type of consideration.
@ref sch 1C para 5 General principles (src:18962-18964)
GIVEN `cash consideration is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has ensured that it can fulfil in full any cash consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other type of consideration is offered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offeror has taken all reasonable measures to secure the implementation of any other type of consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 5 the offeror is barred from announcing the takeover bid yet` MEANS
    IF       (`cash consideration is offered` AND NOT (`the offeror has ensured that it can fulfil in full any cash consideration`))
         OR  (`any other type of consideration is offered` AND NOT (`the offeror has taken all reasonable measures to secure the implementation of any other type of consideration`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An offeror must announce a takeover bid only after— (a) ensuring ..., and (b) taking all reasonable measures ..." (the "only after" is met)

-- src:18965 | 6 An offeree company must not be hindered in the conduct of its affairs for longer than is reasonable by a takeover bid for its securities.
@ref sch 1C para 6 General principles (src:18965)
GIVEN `the offeree company is hindered in the conduct of its affairs by a takeover bid for its securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is for longer than is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 6 the hindrance of the offeree company is barred` MEANS
    IF `the offeree company is hindered in the conduct of its affairs by a takeover bid for its securities` AND `that is for longer than is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for longer than is reasonable"

