-- PART 2: OTHER PROVISION (paragraphs 7 to 19)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---- paragraphs 7 to 10: the mandatory takeover bid, the equitable price, the consideration --------------------

-- src:18972 | (3) Rules must ensure that where control has been acquired following a voluntary takeover bid to all the holders of securities for all their holdings, the obligation referred to in sub-paragraph (1) to make a mandatory takeover bid no longer applies.
@ref sch 1C para 7(3) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18972)
GIVEN `control has been acquired following a voluntary takeover bid to all the holders of securities for all their holdings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 7(3) the obligation to make a mandatory takeover bid no longer applies` MEANS
    IF `control has been acquired following a voluntary takeover bid to all the holders of securities for all their holdings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where control has been acquired following a voluntary takeover bid to all the holders of securities for all their holdings, the obligation referred to in sub-paragraph (1) ... no longer applies" (a failed "where")

-- src:18968 | 7 (1) Rules must ensure that a person (“P”) is required to make a takeover bid (“a mandatory takeover bid”) where—
-- src:18969 | (a) P, or any person acting in concert with P, has acquired securities in a company, and
-- src:18970 | (b) the acquired securities, when added to any existing securities held by P or by persons acting in concert with P, directly or indirectly give P control of that company.
@ref sch 1C para 7(1) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18968-18970)
GIVEN `P, or any person acting in concert with P, has acquired securities in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acquired securities, when added to any existing securities held by P or by persons acting in concert with P, directly or indirectly give P control of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation no longer applies under sub-paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 7(1) the rules must require P to make a mandatory takeover bid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the obligation no longer applies under sub-paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the obligation referred to in sub-paragraph (1) to make a mandatory takeover bid no longer applies"
        IF `P, or any person acting in concert with P, has acquired securities in a company` AND `the acquired securities, when added to any existing securities held by P or by persons acting in concert with P, directly or indirectly give P control of that company`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rules must ensure that a person (“P”) is required to make a takeover bid (“a mandatory takeover bid”) where— (a) ..., and (b) ..." (a failed "where")

-- src:18971 | (2) Rules must ensure that the mandatory takeover bid must be addressed at the earliest opportunity to all of the holders of those securities for all their holdings at the equitable price.
@ref sch 1C para 7(2) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18971)
GIVEN `a mandatory takeover bid is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bid is addressed at the earliest opportunity to all of the holders of those securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bid is for all their holdings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bid is at the equitable price` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 7(2) the mandatory takeover bid meets the requirement the rules must ensure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a mandatory takeover bid is required`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the mandatory takeover bid must be addressed"
        IF `the bid is addressed at the earliest opportunity to all of the holders of those securities` AND `the bid is for all their holdings` AND `the bid is at the equitable price`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the mandatory takeover bid must be addressed at the earliest opportunity to all of the holders of those securities for all their holdings at the equitable price" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `sch 1C para 8(1) purchase` HAS
    `sch 1C para 8(1) date of the purchase` IS A DATE
    `sch 1C para 8(1) price paid` IS A NUMBER
    `sch 1C para 8(1) made by the offeror or by a person acting in concert with the offeror` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sch 1C para 8(1) of the same securities` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN prices IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1C para 8 the highest of the prices` MEANS
    CONSIDER prices
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN max first (`sch 1C para 8 the highest of the prices` rest)

-- (1): "the highest price paid for the same securities by the offeror, or by persons acting in concert with the offeror,
-- over a period, determined by rules, of not less than 6 and not more than 12 months before the mandatory takeover bid
-- is announced". A purchase is within the period if its date is before the announcement and its date plus the period
-- (in months) is not before the announcement. (Fork F10 in NOTES.md.)
-- src:18973 | 8 (1) For the purposes of paragraph 7, “the equitable price” is the highest price paid for the same securities by the offeror, or by persons acting in concert with the offeror, over a period, determined by rules, of not less than 6 and not more than 12 months before the mandatory takeover bid is announced.
@ref sch 1C para 8(1) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18973)
GIVEN purchases IS A LIST OF `sch 1C para 8(1) purchase`
      `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced` IS A DATE
      `the period determined by rules, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1C para 8(1) the equitable price` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the period determined by rules, in months` LESS THAN 6 OR `the period determined by rules, in months` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "over a period, determined by rules, of not less than 6 and not more than 12 months": the rules' period is outside what the paragraph allows
        IF null qualifying
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no purchase by the offeror or a person acting in concert falls in the period, and the paragraph gives no price then
        OTHERWISE JUST (`sch 1C para 8 the highest of the prices` (map price qualifying))
    WHERE
        qualifying MEANS filter isQualifying purchases
        isQualifying p MEANS
                p's `sch 1C para 8(1) made by the offeror or by a person acting in concert with the offeror`
            AND p's `sch 1C para 8(1) of the same securities`
            AND p's `sch 1C para 8(1) date of the purchase` LESS THAN `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced`
            AND `add months` (p's `sch 1C para 8(1) date of the purchase`) `the period determined by rules, in months` AT LEAST `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced`
        price p MEANS p's `sch 1C para 8(1) price paid`

-- src:18974 | (2) Rules must ensure that if, after the mandatory takeover bid has been made public and before the offer closes for acceptance, the offeror or any person acting in concert with the offeror purchases securities at a price higher than the offer price, the offeror must increase the offer consideration so that it is not less than the highest price paid for the securities so acquired.
@ref sch 1C para 8(2) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18974)
GIVEN `the offer price` IS A NUMBER
      `the prices at which the offeror or persons acting in concert purchased securities after the mandatory takeover bid was made public and before the offer closes for acceptance` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1C para 8(2) the offer consideration must not be less than` MEANS
    max `the offer price` (`sch 1C para 8 the highest of the prices` `the prices at which the offeror or persons acting in concert purchased securities after the mandatory takeover bid was made public and before the offer closes for acceptance`)

-- src:18976 | (4) Rules must ensure that any decision by the Panel to adjust the equitable price must be substantiated and made public.
@ref sch 1C para 8(4) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18976)
GIVEN `the decision by the Panel to adjust the equitable price is substantiated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is made public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 8(4) the Panel's decision to adjust the equitable price meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the decision by the Panel to adjust the equitable price is substantiated` AND `the decision is made public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any decision by the Panel to adjust the equitable price must be substantiated and made public" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `sch 1C para 9(1) consideration` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 9(1)(a) securities`
    `sch 1C para 9(1)(b) cash`
    `sch 1C para 9(1)(c) a combination of securities and cash`
    `sch 1C para 9(1) another form of consideration`

-- src:18977 | 9 (1) Rules must ensure that the offeror may offer by way of consideration for the securities which are the subject of the mandatory takeover bid—
-- src:18978 | (a) securities,
-- src:18979 | (b) cash, or
-- src:18980 | (c) a combination of both.
@ref sch 1C para 9(1) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18977-18980)
GIVEN consideration IS A `sch 1C para 9(1) consideration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 9(1) the rules must ensure that the offeror may offer the consideration for the securities` MEANS
    CONSIDER consideration
    WHEN `sch 1C para 9(1) another form of consideration` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the forms in (a) to (c) are not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): the relevant period begins when the period of 8(1) begins and ends when the offer closes for acceptance.
-- src:18984 | (3) “A relevant period” is a period—
-- src:18985 | (a) beginning at the same time as the period determined in accordance with paragraph 8(1), and
-- src:18986 | (b) ending when the offer closes for acceptance.
@ref sch 1C para 9(3) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18984-18986)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced` IS A DATE
      `the period determined by rules, in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the offer closes for acceptance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 9(3) the day is within the relevant period` MEANS
    IF `add months` `the day` `the period determined by rules, in months` AT LEAST `the day the mandatory takeover bid is announced` AND `the day` AT MOST `the day the offer closes for acceptance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“A relevant period” is a period— (a) beginning at the same time as the period determined in accordance with paragraph 8(1), and (b) ending when the offer closes for acceptance" (a day outside it)

-- src:18981 | (2) Rules must ensure that cash must be offered—
-- src:18982 | (a) as an alternative where the consideration offered does not consist of liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market, and
-- src:18983 | (b) at least as an alternative where the securities purchased for cash over a relevant period by the offeror or by persons acting in concert with the offeror, taken together, carry 5% or more of the voting rights in the offeree company.
@ref sch 1C para 9(2) Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18981-18983)
GIVEN `the consideration offered does not consist of liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the voting rights in the offeree company carried by the securities purchased for cash over a relevant period by the offeror or by persons acting in concert with the offeror, taken together` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 9(2) the rules must ensure that cash is offered as an alternative` MEANS
    IF `the consideration offered does not consist of liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` OR `the fraction of the voting rights in the offeree company carried by the securities purchased for cash over a relevant period by the offeror or by persons acting in concert with the offeror, taken together` AT LEAST 0.05
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rules must ensure that cash must be offered— (a) as an alternative where the consideration offered does not consist of liquid securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market, and (b) at least as an alternative where the securities purchased for cash ... carry 5% or more of the voting rights" (a failed "where")

-- src:18988 | 10 Any rules that make provision to protect the interests of the holders of securities that goes beyond the provision referred to in paragraphs 7 to 9 must not hinder the normal course of a takeover bid.
@ref sch 1C para 10 Protection of minority shareholders, the mandatory takeover bid and the equitable price (src:18988)
GIVEN `the rule makes provision to protect the interests of the holders of securities that goes beyond the provision referred to in paragraphs 7 to 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rule hinders the normal course of a takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 10 the rule is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the rule makes provision to protect the interests of the holders of securities that goes beyond the provision referred to in paragraphs 7 to 9`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any rules that make provision to protect the interests of the holders of securities that goes beyond the provision referred to in paragraphs 7 to 9"
        IF `the rule hinders the normal course of a takeover bid`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not hinder the normal course of a takeover bid" (the rule does not hinder it)

-- ---- paragraphs 11 to 14: information, the offer document, time for acceptance --------------------------------------

-- src:18990 | 11 (1) Rules must ensure that a decision to make a takeover bid must be made public without delay and the Panel must be informed of the bid.
@ref sch 1C para 11(1) Information concerning takeover bids (src:18990)
GIVEN `the decision to make a takeover bid has been made public without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Panel has been informed of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 11(1) the decision to make a takeover bid has been made public and the Panel informed as the rules must ensure` MEANS
    IF `the decision to make a takeover bid has been made public without delay` AND `the Panel has been informed of the bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a decision to make a takeover bid must be made public without delay and the Panel must be informed of the bid" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:18992 | (3) Rules must ensure that, as soon as the takeover bid has been made public, the boards of directors of the offeree company and of the offeror must inform—
-- src:18993 | (a) the representatives of their respective employees, or
-- src:18994 | (b) where there are no such representatives, the employees themselves.
@ref sch 1C para 11(3) Information concerning takeover bids (src:18992-18994)
GIVEN `the takeover bid has been made public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are representatives of the respective employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 1C who is told on behalf of the employees`
`sch 1C para 11(3) the boards of the offeree company and of the offeror must inform` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the takeover bid has been made public`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as soon as the takeover bid has been made public"
        IF `there are representatives of the respective employees`
            THEN JUST `sch 1C the representatives of the employees`
        OTHERWISE JUST `sch 1C the employees themselves`

-- src:18995 | 12 (1) Rules must ensure that an offeror must draw up and make public in good time an offer document containing the information necessary to enable the holders of the offeree company’s securities to reach a properly informed decision on the takeover bid.
@ref sch 1C para 12(1) Information concerning takeover bids (src:18995)
GIVEN `the offeror has drawn up and made public in good time an offer document containing the information necessary to enable the holders of the offeree company's securities to reach a properly informed decision on the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 12(1) the offeror has met the requirement to draw up and make public an offer document` MEANS
    IF `the offeror has drawn up and made public in good time an offer document containing the information necessary to enable the holders of the offeree company's securities to reach a properly informed decision on the takeover bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offeror must draw up and make public in good time an offer document containing the information necessary" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:18996 | (2) Rules must ensure that, before the offer document is made public, the offeror must provide a copy to the Panel.
@ref sch 1C para 12(2) Information concerning takeover bids (src:18996)
GIVEN `the offeror provided a copy of the offer document to the Panel before the offer document was made public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 12(2) the offeror has met the requirement to provide a copy to the Panel before the offer document is made public` MEANS
    IF `the offeror provided a copy of the offer document to the Panel before the offer document was made public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the offer document is made public, the offeror must provide a copy to the Panel" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:18997 | (3) Rules must ensure that, when the offer document is made public, the boards of directors of the offeree company and of the offeror must communicate it—
-- src:18998 | (a) to the representatives of their respective employees, or
-- src:18999 | (b) where there are no such representatives, to the employees themselves.
@ref sch 1C para 12(3) Information concerning takeover bids (src:18997-18999)
GIVEN `the offer document has been made public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are representatives of the respective employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 1C who is told on behalf of the employees`
`sch 1C para 12(3) the boards of the offeree company and of the offeror must communicate the offer document to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offer document has been made public`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when the offer document is made public"
        IF `there are representatives of the respective employees`
            THEN JUST `sch 1C the representatives of the employees`
        OTHERWISE JUST `sch 1C the employees themselves`

DECLARE `sch 1C para 12(4) item` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(a) the terms of the takeover bid`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(b) the identity of the offeror and, where the offeror is a company, the company's type, name and registered office`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(c) the securities or, where appropriate, the class or classes of securities for which the takeover bid is made`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(d) the consideration offered for each security or class of securities and, in the case of a mandatory takeover bid, the method employed in determining it, with particulars of the way in which that consideration is to be paid`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(e) the compensation offered for the rights which might be removed as a result of a company's opting-in resolution under Chapter 2, with particulars of the way in which that compensation is to be paid and the method employed in determining it`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(f) the maximum and minimum percentages or quantities of securities which the offeror undertakes to acquire`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(g) details of any existing holdings of the offeror, and of any person acting in concert with the offeror, in the offeree company`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(h) all the conditions to which the takeover bid is subject`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(i) the offeror's intentions with regard to the future business of the offeree company`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(j) the offeror's intentions with regard to the safeguarding of the jobs of the employees and management of the offeree company, including any material change in the conditions of employment`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(k) the offeror's strategic plans for the offeree company, and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of the company's places of business`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(l) if the offeror is a company and in so far as it is affected by the takeover bid, its intentions as to future business and jobs and its strategic plans for itself`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(m) the time allowed for acceptance of the takeover bid`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(n) where the consideration offered includes securities of any kind, information concerning those securities`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(o) information concerning the financing for the takeover bid`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(p) the identity of persons acting in concert with the offeror or with the offeree company and, in the case of companies, the types, names, registered offices and relationships with the offeror and, where possible, with the offeree company`
    `sch 1C para 12(4)(q) the national law which will govern contracts concluded between the offeror and the holders of the offeree company's securities as a result of the takeover bid and the competent courts`

-- (4): "must state at least" (a) to (q): the document meets the minimum if every item that applies to this bid is stated.
-- src:19000 | (4) Rules must ensure that the offer document must state at least—
-- src:19001 | (a) the terms of the takeover bid,
-- src:19002 | (b) the identity of the offeror and, where the offeror is a company, the company’s type, name and registered office,
-- src:19003 | (c) the securities or, where appropriate, the class or classes of securities for which the takeover bid is made,
-- src:19004 | (d) the consideration offered for each security or class of securities and, in the case of a mandatory takeover bid, the method employed in determining it, with particulars of the way in which that consideration is to be paid,
-- src:19005 | (e) the compensation offered for the rights which might be removed as a result of a company’s opting-in resolution under Chapter 2, with particulars of the way in which that compensation is to be paid and the method employed in determining it,
-- src:19006 | (f) the maximum and minimum percentages or quantities of securities which the offeror undertakes to acquire,
-- src:19007 | (g) details of any existing holdings of the offeror, and of any person acting in concert with the offeror, in the offeree company,
-- src:19008 | (h) all the conditions to which the takeover bid is subject,
-- src:19009 | (i) the offeror’s intentions with regard to the future business of the offeree company,
-- src:19010 | (j) the offeror’s intentions with regard to the safeguarding of the jobs of the employees and management of the offeree company, including any material change in the conditions of employment,
-- src:19011 | (k) the offeror’s strategic plans for the offeree company, and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of the company’s places of business,
-- src:19012 | (l) if the offeror is a company and in so far as it is affected by the takeover bid—
-- src:19013 | (i) the offeror’s intentions with regard to its future business,
-- src:19014 | (ii) the offeror’s intentions with regard to the safeguarding of the jobs of its employees and management, including any material change in the conditions of employment, and
-- src:19015 | (iii) the offeror’s strategic plans for itself, and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of its places of business,
-- src:19016 | (m) the time allowed for acceptance of the takeover bid,
-- src:19017 | (n) where the consideration offered includes securities of any kind, information concerning those securities,
-- src:19018 | (o) information concerning the financing for the takeover bid,
-- src:19019 | (p) the identity of persons acting in concert with the offeror or with the offeree company and, in the case of companies, the types, names, registered offices and relationships with the offeror and, where possible, with the offeree company, and
-- src:19020 | (q) the national law which will govern contracts concluded between the offeror and the holders of the offeree company’s securities as a result of the takeover bid and the competent courts.
@ref sch 1C para 12(4) Information concerning takeover bids (src:19000-19020)
GIVEN `the items the offer document does not state` IS A LIST OF `sch 1C para 12(4) item`
      `the items that do not apply to this takeover bid` IS A LIST OF `sch 1C para 12(4) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 12(4) the offer document states at least the information the rules must require` MEANS
    IF null (filter (GIVEN i YIELD NOT (elem i `the items that do not apply to this takeover bid`)) `the items the offer document does not state`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offer document must state at least— (a) ... (q)" (an item that applies is not stated)

-- src:19022 | 13 (1) Rules must ensure that, subject to any provision made in accordance with paragraph 14, the time allowed for the acceptance of a takeover bid must not be less than the period of two weeks nor more than the period of 10 weeks beginning with the day after the date of publication of the offer document.
@ref sch 1C para 13(1) Time allowed for acceptance (src:19022)
GIVEN `the day of publication of the offer document` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the takeover bid is open for acceptance` IS A DATE
      `provision made in accordance with paragraph 14 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 13(1) the time allowed for acceptance is within the limits the rules must ensure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `provision made in accordance with paragraph 14 applies`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any provision made in accordance with paragraph 14"
        IF       `the last day on which the takeover bid is open for acceptance` AT LEAST (`the day of publication of the offer document` PLUS 14)
             AND `the last day on which the takeover bid is open for acceptance` AT MOST (`the day of publication of the offer document` PLUS 70)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the time allowed for the acceptance of a takeover bid must not be less than the period of two weeks nor more than the period of 10 weeks beginning with the day after the date of publication of the offer document" (counting: fork F8)

-- ---- paragraphs 15 and 16: disclosure ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `sch 1C para 15 company` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 15(a) the offeree company`
    `sch 1C para 15(b) the offeror, if the offeror is a company`
    `sch 1C para 15(c) any other company affected by the takeover bid`
    `sch 1C para 15 another person`

-- src:19027 | 15 Rules must ensure that a takeover bid must be made public in such a way as to ensure market transparency and integrity for the securities of—
-- src:19028 | (a) the offeree company,
-- src:19029 | (b) if the offeror is a company, that company, or
-- src:19030 | (c) any other company affected by the takeover bid,
-- src:19031 | in particular in order to prevent the publication or dissemination of false or misleading information.
@ref sch 1C para 15 Disclosure (src:19027-19031)
GIVEN company IS A `sch 1C para 15 company`
      `the offeror is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 15 the rules must ensure that the takeover bid is made public so as to ensure market transparency and integrity for the securities of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER company
    WHEN `sch 1C para 15(a) the offeree company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1C para 15(b) the offeror, if the offeror is a company` THEN
        IF `the offeror is a company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the offeror is a company, that company" (a failed "if")
    WHEN `sch 1C para 15(c) any other company affected by the takeover bid` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1C para 15 another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the securities of— (a) the offeree company, (b) ..., or (c) any other company affected by the takeover bid"

DECLARE `sch 1C para 16 recipient` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 16(a) a holder of securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market who is located in the United Kingdom`
    `sch 1C para 16(b) a representative of the employees of the offeree company or of the offeror`
    `sch 1C para 16(b) an employee of the offeree company or of the offeror, where there are no such representatives`
    `sch 1C para 16 another person`

-- src:19032 | 16 Rules must ensure that all information and documents required by provision made in accordance with paragraphs 11 and 12 must be disclosed in such a manner as to ensure that they are both readily and promptly available—
-- src:19033 | (a) to the holders of securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market who are located in the United Kingdom, and
-- src:19034 | (b) to the representatives of the employees of the offeree company and of the offeror, or where there are no such representatives, to the employees themselves.
@ref sch 1C para 16 Disclosure (src:19032-19034)
GIVEN recipient IS A `sch 1C para 16 recipient`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 16 the rules must ensure that the information and documents are readily and promptly available to the recipient` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `sch 1C para 16 another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the recipients in (a) and (b) are not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- paragraphs 17 and 18: the board of the offeree company -------------------------------------------------------------

-- (2): the relevant period begins when the board receives the information that a decision to make a bid has been made
-- public, or at such earlier stage as rules may determine, and ends when the result is made public or the bid lapses.
-- src:19039 | (2) “The relevant period”—
-- src:19040 | (a) begins when the board of directors of the offeree company receives the information that a decision to make a takeover bid has been made public, or at such earlier stage as rules may determine, and
-- src:19041 | (b) ends when the result of the bid is made public or the bid lapses.
@ref sch 1C para 17(2) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19039-19041)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day the board receives the information that a decision to make a takeover bid has been made public` IS A DATE
      `an earlier stage that rules determine` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the result of the bid is made public or the bid lapses` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 17(2) the day is within the relevant period` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST startDay AND endsAfter
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“The relevant period”— (a) begins when the board ... receives the information ..., or at such earlier stage as rules may determine, and (b) ends when the result of the bid is made public or the bid lapses"
    WHERE
        startDay MEANS
            CONSIDER `an earlier stage that rules determine`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the board receives the information that a decision to make a takeover bid has been made public`
            WHEN JUST earlier THEN
                IF earlier AT MOST `the day the board receives the information that a decision to make a takeover bid has been made public`
                THEN earlier
                ELSE `the day the board receives the information that a decision to make a takeover bid has been made public`
        endsAfter MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the result of the bid is made public or the bid lapses`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST ended THEN `the day` AT MOST ended

-- src:19036 | 17 (1) Rules must ensure that, during the relevant period, the board of directors of the offeree company must obtain the prior authorisation of a general meeting of the company given for this purpose—
-- src:19037 | (a) before taking any action, other than seeking alternative takeover bids, which may result in the frustration of the bid, and
-- src:19038 | (b) in particular, before issuing any shares which may result in a lasting impediment to the offeror’s acquiring control of the offeree company.
@ref sch 1C para 17(1) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19036-19038)
GIVEN `the day is within the relevant period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the board is seeking alternative takeover bids` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action may result in the frustration of the bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is issuing shares which may result in a lasting impediment to the offeror's acquiring control of the offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 17(1) the rules must require the board to obtain the prior authorisation of a general meeting` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day is within the relevant period` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the day is within the relevant period is not answered
        IF `the day is within the relevant period` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the relevant period, the board of directors of the offeree company must obtain the prior authorisation" (a day outside the period: fork F9 in NOTES.md)
        IF `the action is issuing shares which may result in a lasting impediment to the offeror's acquiring control of the offeree company`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the board is seeking alternative takeover bids`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before taking any action, other than seeking alternative takeover bids, which may result in the frustration of the bid" (the excepted action)
        IF `the action may result in the frustration of the bid`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any action ... which may result in the frustration of the bid"

-- src:19042 | (3) Rules must ensure that, with regard to decisions taken before the beginning of the relevant period and not yet partly or fully implemented, a general meeting of the company must approve or confirm any decision—
-- src:19043 | (a) which does not form part of the normal course of the company’s business, and
-- src:19044 | (b) the implementation of which may result in the frustration of the takeover bid.
@ref sch 1C para 17(3) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19042-19044)
GIVEN `the decision was taken before the beginning of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is not yet partly or fully implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision does not form part of the normal course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the implementation of the decision may result in the frustration of the takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 17(3) the rules must require a general meeting to approve or confirm the decision` MEANS
    IF       `the decision was taken before the beginning of the relevant period`
         AND `the decision is not yet partly or fully implemented`
         AND `the decision does not form part of the normal course of the company's business`
         AND `the implementation of the decision may result in the frustration of the takeover bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with regard to decisions taken before the beginning of the relevant period and not yet partly or fully implemented, a general meeting of the company must approve or confirm any decision— (a) which does not form part of the normal course of the company's business, and (b) the implementation of which may result in the frustration of the takeover bid" (a failed condition)

DECLARE `sch 1C para 17(4) body` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 17(4) the management board`
    `sch 1C para 17(4) the supervisory board`
    `sch 1C para 17(4) another body`

-- src:19045 | (4) For the purposes of this paragraph, where a company has a two-tier board structure, “board of directors” means both the management board and the supervisory board.
@ref sch 1C para 17(4) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19045)
GIVEN `the company has a two-tier board structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `sch 1C para 17(4) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 17(4) the body is the board of directors for paragraph 17` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the company has a two-tier board structure`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a company has a two-tier board structure, “board of directors” means both the management board and the supervisory board" (a failed "where")
        IF body EQUALS `sch 1C para 17(4) another body`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“board of directors” means both the management board and the supervisory board"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:19046 | 18 (1) Rules must ensure that the board of directors of the offeree company must draw up and make public a document setting out its opinion of the takeover bid and the reasons for the opinion, including its views on—
-- src:19047 | (a) the effects of implementation of the takeover bid on all the company’s interests and specifically employment, and
-- src:19048 | (b) the offeror’s strategic plans for the offeree company and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of the company’s places of business as set out in the offer document in accordance with paragraph 12(4)(k).
@ref sch 1C para 18(1) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19046-19048)
GIVEN `the board has drawn up and made public a document setting out its opinion of the takeover bid and the reasons for the opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document includes its views on the effects of implementation of the takeover bid on all the company's interests and specifically employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document includes its views on the offeror's strategic plans for the offeree company and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of the company's places of business as set out in the offer document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 18(1) the board has met the requirement to draw up and make public its opinion` MEANS
    IF       `the board has drawn up and made public a document setting out its opinion of the takeover bid and the reasons for the opinion`
         AND `the document includes its views on the effects of implementation of the takeover bid on all the company's interests and specifically employment`
         AND `the document includes its views on the offeror's strategic plans for the offeree company and their likely repercussions on employment and the locations of the company's places of business as set out in the offer document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the board of directors of the offeree company must draw up and make public a document setting out its opinion of the takeover bid and the reasons for the opinion, including its views on (a) ... and (b) ..." (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:19049 | (2) Rules must ensure that the board of directors of the offeree company must at the same time communicate that opinion—
-- src:19050 | (a) to the representatives of its employees, or
-- src:19051 | (b) where there are no such representatives, to the employees themselves.
@ref sch 1C para 18(2) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19049-19051)
GIVEN `the board makes public its opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are representatives of its employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 1C who is told on behalf of the employees`
`sch 1C para 18(2) the board must at the same time communicate its opinion to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the board makes public its opinion`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the same time communicate that opinion"
        IF `there are representatives of its employees`
            THEN JUST `sch 1C the representatives of the employees`
        OTHERWISE JUST `sch 1C the employees themselves`

-- src:19052 | (3) Rules must ensure that, where the board of directors of the offeree company receives in good time a separate opinion from the representatives of its employees on the effects of the takeover bid on employment, that opinion must be appended to the document.
@ref sch 1C para 18(3) Obligations of the board of directors of the offeree company (src:19052)
GIVEN `the board receives in good time a separate opinion from the representatives of its employees on the effects of the takeover bid on employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 18(3) the employees' representatives' opinion must be appended to the document` MEANS
    IF `the board receives in good time a separate opinion from the representatives of its employees on the effects of the takeover bid on employment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the board of directors of the offeree company receives in good time a separate opinion from the representatives of its employees on the effects of the takeover bid on employment, that opinion must be appended to the document" (a failed "where")

-- ---- paragraph 19: other rules applicable to the conduct of takeover bids --------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `sch 1C para 19 topic` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 19(a) the lapsing of takeover bids`
    `sch 1C para 19(b) the revision of takeover bids`
    `sch 1C para 19(c) competing takeover bids`
    `sch 1C para 19(d) the disclosure of the results of takeover bids`
    `sch 1C para 19(e) the irrevocability of takeover bids and the conditions permitted`
    `sch 1C para 19 another topic`

-- src:19054 | 19 Rules must make provision governing the conduct of takeover bids which must address at least—
-- src:19055 | (a) the lapsing of takeover bids,
-- src:19056 | (b) the revision of takeover bids,
-- src:19057 | (c) competing takeover bids,
-- src:19058 | (d) the disclosure of the results of takeover bids, and
-- src:19059 | (e) the irrevocability of takeover bids and the conditions permitted.
@ref sch 1C para 19 Other rules applicable to the conduct of takeover bids (src:19054-19059)
GIVEN topic IS A `sch 1C para 19 topic`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 19 the rules must make provision on the topic` MEANS
    CONSIDER topic
    WHEN `sch 1C para 19 another topic` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "must address at least" (a) to (e)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 20: interpretation
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19062 | “offer document” means a document required to be published by rules made in accordance with paragraph 12;
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061-19062)
GIVEN `it is a document required to be published by rules made in accordance with paragraph 12` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the document is an offer document` MEANS
    IF `it is a document required to be published by rules made in accordance with paragraph 12`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“offer document” means a document required to be published by rules made in accordance with paragraph 12"

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19063 | “offeree company” means a company, the securities of which are the subject of a takeover bid;
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061 and src:19063)
GIVEN `it is a company, the securities of which are the subject of a takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the company is an offeree company` MEANS
    IF `it is a company, the securities of which are the subject of a takeover bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“offeree company” means a company, the securities of which are the subject of a takeover bid"

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19064 | “offeror”, in relation to a takeover bid, means the person making the bid;
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061 and src:19064)
GIVEN `the person is making the bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the person is the offeror in relation to the takeover bid` MEANS
    IF `the person is making the bid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“offeror”, in relation to a takeover bid, means the person making the bid"

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19065 | “rules” means rules made by the Panel under section 943(1);
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061 and src:19065)
GIVEN `they are rules made by the Panel under section 943(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the rules are rules for this Schedule` MEANS
    IF `they are rules made by the Panel under section 943(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“rules” means rules made by the Panel under section 943(1)"

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19066 | “securities” means transferable securities carrying voting rights in a company;
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061 and src:19066)
GIVEN `they are transferable securities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `they carry voting rights in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the instruments are securities` MEANS
    IF NOT (`they carry voting rights in a company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“securities” means transferable securities carrying voting rights in a company"
    ELSE CONSIDER `they are transferable securities`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "“securities” means transferable securities" (transferable securities has the meaning given by Article 2.1.24 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014: section 1173(1))
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "transferable securities" is defined by an EU Regulation that is not among the sources

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19067 | “takeover bid” means a public offer made to the holders of the securities of a company to acquire some or all of those securities, whether mandatory or voluntary, which follows or has as its objective the acquisition of control of that company, but does not include cases where the offer is made by the company itself;
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061 and src:19067)
GIVEN `it is a public offer made to the holders of the securities of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made to acquire some or all of those securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it follows, or has as its objective, the acquisition of control of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is made by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offer is made by the company itself`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include cases where the offer is made by the company itself"
        IF `it is a public offer made to the holders of the securities of a company` AND `it is made to acquire some or all of those securities` AND `it follows, or has as its objective, the acquisition of control of that company`
            THEN JUST TRUE -- "whether mandatory or voluntary": the kind of bid makes no difference
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“takeover bid” means a public offer made to the holders of the securities of a company to acquire some or all of those securities ... which follows or has as its objective the acquisition of control of that company"

-- src:19061 | 20 (1) In this Schedule—
-- src:19068 | “voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question.
@ref sch 1C para 20(1) Interpretation (src:19061 and src:19068)
GIVEN `they are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(1) the rights are voting rights for this Schedule` MEANS
    IF `they are rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“voting rights” means rights to vote at general meetings of the company in question"

-- src:19070 | (3) In this Schedule, “persons acting in concert” means persons who co-operate with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding aimed at—
-- src:19071 | (a) acquiring control of the offeree company, or
-- src:19072 | (b) frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid.
@ref sch 1C para 20(3) Interpretation (src:19070-19072)
GIVEN `the person co-operates with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that agreement or understanding is aimed at acquiring control of the offeree company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that agreement or understanding is aimed at frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(3) the person is a person acting in concert` MEANS
    IF `the person co-operates with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding` AND (`that agreement or understanding is aimed at acquiring control of the offeree company` OR `that agreement or understanding is aimed at frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“persons acting in concert” means persons who co-operate with the offeror or the offeree company on the basis of an agreement or understanding aimed at— (a) acquiring control of the offeree company, or (b) frustrating the successful outcome of a takeover bid"

DECLARE `sch 1C para 20(4) pair` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1C para 20(4)(a) A and B`
    `sch 1C para 20(4)(a) A and another subsidiary undertaking of B`
    `sch 1C para 20(4)(b) B and A`
    `sch 1C para 20(4)(b) another subsidiary undertaking of B and A`
    `sch 1C para 20(4) any other pair`

-- src:19073 | (4) For the purposes of this Schedule, where a person (“A”) is a subsidiary undertaking of another person (“B”) within the meaning of section 420 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (but disregarding subsections (2)(b) and (3) of that section, and subsections (2)(c) and (4)(b) of section 1162 of the Companies Act 2006)—
-- src:19074 | (a) A is deemed to be acting in concert with B and with any other subsidiary undertakings of B, and
-- src:19075 | (b) B and those subsidiary undertakings are deemed to be acting in concert with A.
@ref sch 1C para 20(4) Interpretation (src:19073-19075)
GIVEN `A is a subsidiary undertaking of B within the meaning of section 420 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (disregarding subsections (2)(b) and (3) of that section, and subsections (2)(c) and (4)(b) of section 1162 of the Companies Act 2006)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      pair IS A `sch 1C para 20(4) pair`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 20(4) the two are deemed to be acting in concert` MEANS
    CONSIDER `A is a subsidiary undertaking of B within the meaning of section 420 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (disregarding subsections (2)(b) and (3) of that section, and subsections (2)(c) and (4)(b) of section 1162 of the Companies Act 2006)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a person (“A”) is a subsidiary undertaking of another person (“B”) within the meaning of section 420 ... A is deemed to be acting in concert with B" (a failed "where")
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 420 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 is not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER pair
        WHEN `sch 1C para 20(4) any other pair` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) A is deemed to be acting in concert with B and with any other subsidiary undertakings of B, and (b) B and those subsidiary undertakings are deemed to be acting in concert with A"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

