-- src:19076 | 21 (1) In this Schedule, other than in the listed provisions, “company” means a company that has securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
@ref sch 1C para 21(1) Interpretation (src:19076)
GIVEN `the provision is one of the listed provisions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body has securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1C para 21(1) the body is a company for this Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision is one of the listed provisions`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than in the listed provisions": there, section 1 does not apply (sub-paragraph (3)) and the Schedule gives no other meaning
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provision is a listed provision is not answered
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the body has securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a company that has securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market"
